    description: "metrics.total_files=916 (= debug.unique_paths_in_analysis) but only 902 file-kind anchor nodes exist. 13 real paths have content nodes (class/method/interface/dependency/project) yet zero file-kind node; the contains tree for those files is rootless at the file level. Anchorless paths (have nodes, no file anchor) = 13: 7x pyproject.toml (toml: project+dependency nodes), 1x package.json (json), csharp/Program.cs, java/Main.java, solidity/Contract.sol, sql/schema.sql, wgsl/shader.wgsl. Example: java/Main.java has 5 nodes {interface, method x2, enum, class} — contains edges INTO them originate from CLASS nodes (IService/MyService), src_is_file_node=False; no file->class root exists. The 916-902=14 gap = 13 anchorless-with-nodes + 1 analyzed-but-zero-node path. Consequence: a consumer walking the contains hierarchy from file roots cannot reach these 13 files' symbols; a consumer counting 'files' off file-kind nodes undercounts by 14 vs metrics.total_files."  # 17c7
